---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const pageTitle = "Welcome";
---
<BaseLayout pageTitle={pageTitle}>
  	<p>
		Welcome to my Astro project for CSE 134B! I built this site to learn how to use
		Astro, experiment with components, layouts, and Markdown content, and create
		a small, organized website.
	</p>

	<p>Here's what you'll find on this site:</p>

	<ol>
		<li><strong>About Page</strong> - A short introduction about me using variables, arrays, and conditional rendering in Astro.</li>
		<li><strong>Blog Page</strong> - A simple blog that lists Markdown posts describing my progress and what I’ve learned.</li>
		<li><strong>Reusable Layouts</strong> - A shared BaseLayout and PostLayout that keep the site consistent.</li>
		<li><strong>Responsive Navigation</strong> - A mobile-friendly menu built for the assignment.</li>
	</ol>

	<p>
		Feel free to explore the site to see how different pages are structured and how
		Astro handles templates and components.
	</p>
</BaseLayout>